<title>BRAZIL: Cia Hering posts 1996 loss of 17.4 mln.</title>
<headline>Cia Hering posts 1996 loss of 17.4 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian holding firm Companhia Hering, which has interests in the textile and foods sectors, published the following consolidated 1996 financial results.</p>
<p>			  1996		1995</p>
<p>Share		    1.46 loss	 0.74 profit</p>
<p>Net		     17.4 million loss     8.77 million profit</p>
<p>Gross Sales	   1.62 bln	   1.4 bln</p>
<p>Gross Profit	  509 million	    459.6 million</p>
<p>Oper Loss		7.8 million	    2.98 million</p>
<p>Note: All figures are in Brazilian reais and not adjusted for inflation. Share loss is per lot of 1,000 shares.</p>
<p>((--James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413))</p>
